    "CPUが考え中…" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "CPU is thinking…"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "CPUと交互に札を取ります。場の札の読みの最後の字から始まる読みの札を選べたら、その札を取れます。取った札が新しい場の札になります" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Take turns with the CPU. Cards are read in Japanese: pick a card whose reading starts with the last kana of the card in play, and it's yours. The card you take becomes the new card in play."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "、山札%lld枚" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : ", stock %lld"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "「%1$@」で終わるときはひとつ前の字で受けます。「%2$@」のような濁音は、そのまま「%2$@」でも、濁点を取った「%3$@」でも受けられます。1枚の札が別の読みを持つこともあります（うらよみ）" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "If a reading ends with “%1$@”, continue from the kana before it. A voiced kana like “%2$@” can be followed by “%2$@” itself or by “%3$@” without the voicing marks. Some cards also have an alternate reading."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "「%@」からはじまる札を取ろう" : {
